  "question": {
    "text": "A thermometer graduated according to a linear scale reads a value $x_{0}$ when in contact with boiling water, and $x_{0} / 3$ when in contact with ice. What is the temperature of an object in ${ }^{\\circ} \\mathrm{C}$, if this thermometer in the contact with the object reads $x_{0} / 2 ?$"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "25",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "60",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "40",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "35",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "A"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "Let required temperature $=\\mathrm{T}^{\\circ} \\mathrm{C}$\r\n\r\n<img src=\"assets\\st0088_365ede882af1.png\"><br>\r\n\r\n$\\Rightarrow \\mathrm{T}^{\\circ} \\mathrm{C}=\\frac{\\mathrm{x}_{0}}{2}-\\frac{\\mathrm{x}_{0}}{3}=\\frac{\\mathrm{x}_{0}}{6}$\r\n\r\n$\\&\\left(\\mathrm{x}_{0}-\\frac{\\mathrm{x}_{0}}{3}\\right)=\\left(100-0^{\\circ} \\mathrm{C}\\right)$\r\n\r\n$\\Rightarrow \\frac{2 \\mathrm{x}_{0}}{3}=100 \\Rightarrow \\mathrm{x}_{0}=\\frac{300}{2}$\r\n\r\n$\\Rightarrow \\mathrm{T}^{\\circ} \\mathrm{C}=\\frac{\\mathrm{x}_{0}}{6}=\\frac{150}{6}=25^{\\circ} \\mathrm{C}$"
  }
}